  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BGD100444 - CoC + Girls Shine CXB - Fifth phase</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will deliver integrated protection and gender-based violence prevention services in Bangladesh, targeting women, girls, and vulnerable populations through a UNFPA-funded annual work plan._x000d_
_x000d_
Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Prevention and Response: The project will provide case management, psychosocial support, and referrals for survivors of violence, alongside strengthening safe spaces and service delivery points to ensure access to confidential and quality GBV services._x000d_
_x000d_
Sexual and Reproductive Health (SRH): Essential SRH services will be supported, including access to reproductive health information, dignity kits, and referrals to health facilities, with a focus on women and adolescent girls._x000d_
_x000d_
Community Engagement and Awareness: Outreach activities will be conducted through community groups and volunteers to raise awareness on GBV prevention, early marriage, and women&#x2019;s rights, promoting behaviour change and service uptake._x000d_
_x000d_
Capacity Strengthening: Training and technical support will be provided to frontline workers, community volunteers, and service providers to improve quality, coordination, and survivor-centred approaches._x000d_
_x000d_
Adolescent and Youth Engagement: The project will support adolescent girls and boys through safe spaces, life skills sessions, and targeted awareness activities to strengthen resilience and reduce protection risks._x000d_
_x000d_
Cash and In-Kind Support: Targeted assistance, including dignity kits and other essential items, will be provided to vulnerable individuals to support immediate needs and dignity._x000d_
_x000d_
The project will be implemented with local partners and in coordination with government and humanitarian actors. It prioritises women, girls, and other at-risk groups, integrating protection, gender, and inclusion across all activities.</narrative>
  </description>
